WEBVTT

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:11.360
"Kodomo no Odocha"

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:13.700
That rumor that I love you

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:17.330
is true, yes it is.

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:20.830
You can't ignore it either.

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:25.420
Whether you're awake or asleep,

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:29.050
please don't be embarrassed.

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:36.590
Is it a sin if I sneak into your heart

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:40.310
by ridding you...

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:43.480
...of your other love?

00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:48.060
At sunset,

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:50.570
when the children go home,

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:54.530
Today's incident is burning love!

00:00:54.650 --> 00:00:58.410
You can tell it accurately.

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:00.490
7 O'Clock News!

00:01:00.830 --> 00:01:04.290
Please, our relationship...

00:01:05.330 --> 00:01:09.960
Please don't blame it on the true kiss

00:01:10.130 --> 00:01:11.800
In a city without light,

00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:15.680
let's burn the fire of love.

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:19.100
Don't be so easy going

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:21.350
The existence is a mistake

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:24.850
You're asking for something not there.

00:01:32.230 --> 00:01:35.900
I'm Kurata Sana,
a 6th grader and TV personality.

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:38.910
My beloved Mama is an
Aoki-award winning novelist.

00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:42.580
Sagami Rei-kun, my chauffeur,
manager, and former boyfriend.

00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:44.580
The mysterious white bat straight man.

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:46.580
My voice is doing fine!

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:49.920
Hayama Akito, my natural enemy
and good friend.

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:52.250
Let me introduce my classmates!
Tsuyoshi-kun and Aya-chan.

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:54.920
These two are head over heels
with each other, the bastards!

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:57.800
Hisae-chan, who's sort of a
traditional Tokyoite, and Mami-chan.

00:01:57.800 --> 00:01:59.760
Today's story is about Mami-chan.

00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:04.430
"A Band-Aid For the Heart?"

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:12.980
Time for gym class!
I'm going to go give it my all!

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:14.980
What is everyone doing over there?

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:16.650
Hey, everyone, what are you doing?

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:18.660
Ah, Sana-chan, it's Kurosuke! Kurosuke!

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:19.660
Croquet?

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:21.320
Ku-ro-su-ke.

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:23.330
Yo, Kurosuke! I don't see him.

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:24.330
Sana-chan!

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:25.330
Yes?

00:02:25.330 --> 00:02:27.370
Sana-chan, do you want to give it a try?

00:02:29.330 --> 00:02:31.830
Oh, how pretty!

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:40.720
--You know, you can give Kurosuke
some water to drink
--Oh, wonderful! Cute! Coquettish! Lovely!

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:43.600
--with this bottle. Want to try?
--Delicious (that would be yucky) Great!
Plate! Empire State Building!

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:44.930
The story moves on!

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:47.270
I can give him water with this?

00:02:47.270 --> 00:02:47.930
Sip!

00:02:47.930 --> 00:02:51.270
Aren't rabbits not
supposed to drink water?

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:53.020
That's just a superstition.

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:55.940
--But you do have to be careful
not to give them too much to drink.
--I'm caught here.

00:02:55.940 --> 00:02:57.440
Really? Okay...

00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:00.280
--Mm-hmm. I also have to be careful
how much watery foods I give him,
--Somebody, get me out.

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:02.950
--or else it will upset his stomach.
--I said I'm caught here.

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:07.620
Wow, I didn't know that you took
such good care of Kurosuke, Mami-chan.

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:10.960
It's almost like you're
Kurosuke's mother, Mami-chan.

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:13.290
I got myself out.

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:15.880
It was my turn when
Kurosuke left the nest,

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:18.630
and Kurosuke was so little
compared to the other bunnies.

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:20.630
Ah, Sana-chan, that's enough.

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:23.300
Oh, okay. If he drinks too much,
he'll get the runs.

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:25.970
Right, right.

00:03:25.970 --> 00:03:27.970
Ah, class is starting!

00:03:27.970 --> 00:03:29.310
Gym! Gym!

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:33.270
That's right, ma'am, the next class
is gym, where you will be jumping rope.

00:03:33.270 --> 00:03:36.270
I forgot my jump rope! I'm going
to go run back to the classroom.

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:37.940
Will you make it in time?

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:40.820
Okay, I'll tell the teacher "There was
a huge herd of sheep crossing the road,

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:42.240
so Mami-chan will be late" for you!

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:43.280
Don't do that!

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:44.570
Why not!?

00:03:44.570 --> 00:03:48.160
Because that doesn't
happen very often in Japan.

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:50.960
Have some?

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:55.920
Don't get too full of yourself,
just because Mami-chan pampers you!

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:59.630
Babbit wants to be pampered, too.

00:03:59.630 --> 00:04:00.380
"6th Grade 3rd Class"

00:04:00.590 --> 00:04:03.840
"Gym time!"

00:04:00.590 --> 00:04:05.340
What a bother. This is what I get
for worrying only about Kurosuke.

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:12.270
Huh? Why am I hiding?

00:04:12.310 --> 00:04:17.400
What? No one's here. I'm sleepy...

00:04:22.950 --> 00:04:26.530
Hayama-kun! I wonder
if he's skipping class.

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:31.410
Never mind him, get the rope.

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:36.040
What are you doing?

00:04:39.590 --> 00:04:41.420
Are you all right?

00:04:43.260 --> 00:04:45.930
Hey...

00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:47.350
No...

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:50.220
Stay back...

00:04:52.930 --> 00:04:54.940
No...

00:04:54.940 --> 00:04:56.310
No!

00:04:57.270 --> 00:04:58.610
Stay back!

00:04:58.610 --> 00:04:59.940
...big herd of cows!

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:01.280
Cows?

00:05:00.980 --> 00:05:02.490
"It's Mami-chan..."

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:02.740
Hmm, I'm worried.

00:05:05.950 --> 00:05:06.950
What's the matter?

00:05:06.950 --> 00:05:08.280
Did something happen to you?

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:08.950
Mm-mm...

00:05:08.950 --> 00:05:10.950
Mami-chan, let's go
to the nurse's office.

00:05:10.950 --> 00:05:11.950
Can you stand?

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:13.290
Hayama!

00:05:13.290 --> 00:05:14.620
What did you do!?

00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:16.920
What did you do to Mami-chan!?

00:05:18.630 --> 00:05:21.920
Mami-chan wouldn't have screamed
if you hadn't done something!

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:23.970
She wouldn't be so scared, you know!

00:05:23.970 --> 00:05:26.630
Let go.

00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:28.720
Let go of me.

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:36.600
Hey, Hayama, you're acting
a little funny, aren't you?

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:39.690
Why don't you tell
your big sister about it?

00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:43.230
All right, I'll shake it out
of you with my Burutcha--!

00:05:43.230 --> 00:05:46.900
This won't do. If you're going
to open it, be sure to close it. Hmm?

00:05:46.900 --> 00:05:50.580
My, what a cute little bat!

00:05:51.910 --> 00:05:52.910
Just kidding.

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:54.250
I'm caught here...

00:05:53.910 --> 00:06:01.420
"Sana doesn't understand?"

00:05:54.250 --> 00:05:56.580
Babbit has just arrived.

00:05:56.580 --> 00:05:59.580
--Babbit-san, I brought my friend.
--Hey, it's the American...

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:01.630
Aloha. I'm Hawaii-Babbit.

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:04.840
I really don't know what's going on.

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:04.630
"Erevest"

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:07.880
It appears that something
happened to Mami-chan,

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:11.600
but there's something wrong
with Hayama, too. I wonder what.

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:14.350
You don't have any idea?

00:06:15.930 --> 00:06:17.850
I don't think that anything has happened

00:06:17.850 --> 00:06:19.940
between Hayama and Mami-chan
since that one incident.

00:06:19.940 --> 00:06:24.940
And afterward, Hayama apologized
for his stupidity. After all this time...

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:29.610
After all this time?

00:06:29.610 --> 00:06:32.910
After... all... this... time...?

00:06:32.910 --> 00:06:36.250
You're the only one who
thinks it's "after all this time."

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:39.250
Do you remember just what happened
when Hayama-kun ran wild?

00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:41.920
He plunged Mami-chan
into that pond, right?

00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:45.590
The boys that Hayama-kun was ordering
around poked at Mami-chan, right?

00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:49.180
Do you know what kind of scars that
leaves on the heart of a little girl

00:06:49.180 --> 00:06:50.590
who has had that happen to her?

00:06:50.590 --> 00:06:53.260
Can you understand that?

00:06:53.260 --> 00:06:55.260
It's frightening. It hurts.

00:06:55.260 --> 00:06:56.970
When the two of them
are alone together,

00:06:56.970 --> 00:07:00.270
she might be reminded sometimes
of what she felt at the time.

00:07:01.940 --> 00:07:05.610
Scars of the heart do not
disappear over a mere apology.

00:07:05.610 --> 00:07:08.610
It's possible that she will
continue to resent Hayama-kun

00:07:08.610 --> 00:07:09.950
for the rest of her life.

00:07:09.950 --> 00:07:13.370
That's just how scars of the heart are.

00:07:15.280 --> 00:07:20.290
So that's it. I thought that
it was all in the past. However,

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:24.960
I guess to Mami-chan, it isn't.

00:07:26.630 --> 00:07:29.050
I'm going out!

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:34.550
Gaah! An avalanche!? Onda! Onda!

00:07:34.550 --> 00:07:35.680
Is this his day off?

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:38.430
"Suzuki"

00:07:41.230 --> 00:07:44.560
So, I'm here at Mami-chan's house,
but what should I say to her?

00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:47.230
Ba-bing, push the button, ba-bing!

00:07:47.230 --> 00:07:48.570
What are you hesitating for,
Kurata Sana!?

00:07:48.570 --> 00:07:49.900
Would you go home
without doing anything!?

00:07:49.900 --> 00:07:52.030
Push it! Push it!

00:07:54.910 --> 00:07:57.580
Excuse me, it's a little to the left...

00:07:57.580 --> 00:07:58.910
That's a strange sound.

00:07:58.910 --> 00:08:00.250
Over there, over there!

00:07:59.870 --> 00:08:03.330
"Stop doing that"

00:08:00.250 --> 00:08:02.580
I can push it. "Ding-dong."

00:08:02.580 --> 00:08:03.580
Oweowe.

00:08:07.590 --> 00:08:08.590
Yes?

00:08:08.590 --> 00:08:10.260
Huh? What is it, Sana-chan?

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:11.920
Babbit is here, too.

00:08:11.920 --> 00:08:15.510
Oh, I see. I went home early, so you
came because you were worried about me.

00:08:15.510 --> 00:08:17.260
Sorry about that. Come on in.

00:08:17.260 --> 00:08:18.260
That's okay, I'll stay here.

00:08:18.260 --> 00:08:19.930
Babbit is okay here, too.

00:08:19.930 --> 00:08:21.930
Are you for sure coming
to school tomorrow?

00:08:21.930 --> 00:08:23.600
Yeah, I'll be fine.

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:25.940
Sure you will. Kurosuke will
be waiting for you, and all.

00:08:25.940 --> 00:08:28.270
Isn't he cute?

00:08:28.270 --> 00:08:31.530
Come on, you were going to talk
about Hayama, right? Come on, come on!

00:08:31.530 --> 00:08:34.860
He's a lot cuter than that strange animal
loitering around over there, huh?

00:08:34.860 --> 00:08:38.240
You say that, and I'm going to grow huge!

00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:43.210
Sana-chan, you idiot!

00:08:43.210 --> 00:08:45.880
Say, Mami-chan...

00:08:45.880 --> 00:08:50.250
Mami-chan, about Hayama...
by any chance--?

00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:53.590
Sana-chan, thanks for coming by today.
I'll see you at school tomorrow!

00:08:53.590 --> 00:08:55.220
Mami-chan...

00:08:55.220 --> 00:08:59.930
Sana-chan, it's okay... Don't worry...

00:08:59.930 --> 00:09:02.220
I'm sorry.

00:09:02.220 --> 00:09:04.600
Sure enough...

00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:07.270
It's just like Mama said.

00:09:07.270 --> 00:09:08.810
She said that just
because you apologized,

00:09:08.810 --> 00:09:11.940
that doesn't mean that
everything up to now is swept away.

00:09:11.940 --> 00:09:15.240
So, Mami-chan must
still be upset about it.

00:09:15.240 --> 00:09:19.280
I mean, you're not the only one
who did that awful thing to Mami-chan,

00:09:19.280 --> 00:09:23.950
but Hayama, you're the one who Mami-chan
is most afraid of. That must be it.

00:09:26.290 --> 00:09:28.830
I think that when you
wound someone's heart,

00:09:28.830 --> 00:09:31.300
it's something that can't be undone.

00:09:31.300 --> 00:09:33.880
"Water spilled does not return
with a bang," and all.

00:09:33.880 --> 00:09:36.880
It's not "bang," it's "basin."

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:38.720
"Water spilled does not
return to the basin,"

00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:41.560
which means that once water is spilled,
you can't put it back the way it was,

00:09:41.560 --> 00:09:44.230
has come to mean something
that cannot be undone.

00:09:44.230 --> 00:09:45.560
Even so,

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:47.730
we're still kids,
and we're still young,

00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:51.570
and maybe if we want to undo something,
it can be undone, right?

00:09:51.570 --> 00:09:55.240
Having Mami-chan resenting Hayama
like this from now on...

00:09:55.240 --> 00:09:57.450
There's absolutely no way
I'm going to have my friends

00:09:57.450 --> 00:09:59.240
resenting and being resented
by each other!

00:09:59.240 --> 00:10:01.580
So what are you going to do?

00:10:01.580 --> 00:10:02.660
"Sana-chan thinks!"

00:10:02.910 --> 00:10:05.250
Happy!

00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:07.250
Whoo! Happy!

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:11.920
♪ Happy, happy, happy, everyone happy, ♪

00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:13.590
♪ chuck away the sadness and the pain, ♪

00:10:13.590 --> 00:10:15.590
♪ have fun singing, enjoy the humor, ♪

00:10:15.590 --> 00:10:17.880
♪ every day is happy, happy, happy! ♪

00:10:21.260 --> 00:10:24.930
♪ Hayama and Mami-chan,
returning water to the basin, ♪

00:10:24.930 --> 00:10:26.600
♪ somehow or other, somehow or other,
somehow or other, somehow or other, ♪

00:10:26.600 --> 00:10:28.600
♪ becoming friends again, happy-py! ♪

00:10:28.600 --> 00:10:30.270
Happy!

00:10:30.270 --> 00:10:33.400
Sana-chan's Mission, Mark I...
I guess you'd call it.

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:35.860
Good morning.

00:10:35.860 --> 00:10:37.530
Mami-chan, are you okay?

00:10:37.530 --> 00:10:38.200
Mm-hmm.

00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:40.870
I don't know what we'd do
if you stayed home, Mami-chan.

00:10:40.870 --> 00:10:44.870
Yeah, that's right.

00:10:44.870 --> 00:10:49.870
Oh, dear. Let's not mention
what happened yesterday!

00:10:49.870 --> 00:10:51.750
Hello!

00:10:53.210 --> 00:10:55.550
Mami-chan, is there a
type of boy that you prefer?

00:10:55.550 --> 00:10:57.550
What's this, out of the blue, Sana-chan?

00:10:57.550 --> 00:11:01.550
Okay! Let me handle it! I know,
how about xxxx-chan from xxxxx?

00:11:01.550 --> 00:11:03.220
Yeah, he's cool!

00:11:03.220 --> 00:11:05.560
Where's xxxx-chan!?
Is he inside that bag!?

00:11:05.560 --> 00:11:08.560
I doubt he would be.

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:10.230
It's xxxx-chan's hair!

00:11:10.230 --> 00:11:11.560
It's just a wig.

00:11:11.560 --> 00:11:13.560
Now for a model...
all right, there's one!

00:11:13.560 --> 00:11:14.900
There is?

00:11:14.900 --> 00:11:16.570
You there, come here a minute.

00:11:16.570 --> 00:11:19.570
We put this on him...

00:11:19.570 --> 00:11:21.740
Yo, Hayama!

00:11:24.580 --> 00:11:26.910
Ah, they're eating it up.

00:11:26.910 --> 00:11:28.250
Sorry!

00:11:28.250 --> 00:11:31.580
Here's this one!

00:11:31.580 --> 00:11:33.580
Okay, how about this one?

00:11:33.580 --> 00:11:35.590
Or this one?

00:11:35.590 --> 00:11:37.590
One more!

00:11:37.590 --> 00:11:39.920
So, which one is best, Mami-chan?

00:11:39.800 --> 00:11:40.800
"Where Mami-chan used to be"

00:11:39.920 --> 00:11:41.260
Huh?

00:11:41.260 --> 00:11:44.260
Mami-chan went to go check on Kurosuke.

00:11:44.260 --> 00:11:45.720
No good, huh?

00:11:51.270 --> 00:11:54.610
A-one, a-two, a-hoy-hoy-hoy-hoy...

00:11:54.610 --> 00:11:55.940
Mami-chan!

00:11:55.940 --> 00:11:58.940
We're the get-along bunnies!

00:11:58.940 --> 00:12:00.950
Well? Are we cute?

00:12:00.950 --> 00:12:02.950
This is kind of fun, huh?

00:12:02.950 --> 00:12:05.950
But I'm starting to get
hot and tired, Sana-chan.

00:12:05.950 --> 00:12:08.370
Mm-hmm! That is cute!

00:12:11.620 --> 00:12:13.960
That really is cute! What fun!

00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:18.130
Let me introduce our members!
Sasaki Tsuyoshi-kun!

00:12:19.630 --> 00:12:21.630
Hayama Akito-kun!

00:12:21.630 --> 00:12:22.300
Huh?

00:12:22.260 --> 00:12:25.640
"Where Hayama used to be"

00:12:22.970 --> 00:12:25.300
No fair running away, Akito-kun.

00:12:25.300 --> 00:12:26.350
Yeah.

00:12:42.030 --> 00:12:45.450
In dreams, my eyes see you in dreams

00:12:51.530 --> 00:12:55.870
Hayama! What good will running away do!?

00:12:55.870 --> 00:12:57.640
Hayama?

00:13:05.540 --> 00:13:06.880
Hey!

00:13:06.880 --> 00:13:11.730
Hayama, don't beat up the school building!
If you don't want to dance, then say so!

00:13:19.560 --> 00:13:21.660
Hayama...

00:13:56.530 --> 00:14:01.120
"Hayama..."

00:13:57.200 --> 00:13:58.700
Whoa...

00:14:00.200 --> 00:14:01.140
Whoa...

00:14:01.530 --> 00:14:03.870
Now you've done it.

00:14:03.870 --> 00:14:05.870
The thing about scars
of the heart, you see,

00:14:05.870 --> 00:14:08.210
is that I doubt you can fix them
by slapping a Heal-Band on them.

00:14:08.210 --> 00:14:11.540
I wonder if your little first aid
treatment wasn't something like that.

00:14:11.540 --> 00:14:14.350
What Hayama-kun did to Mami-chan

00:14:14.350 --> 00:14:16.590
was something he absolutely
should not have done.

00:14:17.550 --> 00:14:22.220
That's something that
Hayama-kun is aware of.

00:14:22.220 --> 00:14:27.220
Ever since Hayama-kun realized "I've done
something that I shouldn't have done,"

00:14:27.260 --> 00:14:29.890
he has had his heart wounded, too.

00:14:29.900 --> 00:14:33.160
You only thought about how Mami-chan
had been hurt, didn't you?

00:14:33.170 --> 00:14:36.170
No matter how many
bandages you have ready,

00:14:36.170 --> 00:14:38.900
you won't be able to provide enough
first aid to either Mami-chan's scars,

00:14:38.900 --> 00:14:40.980
or to Hayama-kun's scars, that way.

00:14:43.180 --> 00:14:46.050
Hayama has been suffering too, huh?

00:14:49.180 --> 00:14:51.520
Isn't there anything I can do?

00:14:51.520 --> 00:14:54.190
Watuh spilled does not
retoin to the basin game!

00:14:54.190 --> 00:14:57.520
Today we're having our first in a series
of poisonally experience with provoibs!

00:14:57.520 --> 00:15:00.790
In this game, that huge basin is gonna
tilt ovuh, making you slip and slip,

00:15:00.790 --> 00:15:02.190
and if you fawl, you're out!

00:15:02.190 --> 00:15:04.860
But if you fawl, look,
there's this cushion!

00:15:04.860 --> 00:15:07.530
It's nice and sawft,
and feels pretty good,

00:15:07.530 --> 00:15:09.570
which means that if you fawl,
you'll be awl right,

00:15:09.570 --> 00:15:11.870
but once you fawl, you can't
get back up into the basin.

00:15:11.870 --> 00:15:16.040
What a hawsh game this is!
Zero! Zero! Zero! Zero!

00:15:16.040 --> 00:15:17.540
Everything's gonna be awl gone!

00:15:17.540 --> 00:15:19.540
Okay, good luck, everyone!

00:15:19.550 --> 00:15:21.210
Oh? Sana-chan's the only one left?

00:15:21.210 --> 00:15:24.550
If I fall, there's no going back.

00:15:24.550 --> 00:15:26.220
Sana-chan, good luck!

00:15:26.220 --> 00:15:28.550
Sana-chan sure is
hanging in there today, huh?

00:15:28.550 --> 00:15:32.160
Ah, hello, Higashiyamato-san.
Oh, what's with the hat and T-shirt?

00:15:32.160 --> 00:15:34.830
Yeah, aren't they nice?
I got them as gifts from New York.

00:15:34.830 --> 00:15:36.160
I bought them for him.

00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:38.160
Yeah, I'm so pleased. Thank you.

00:15:38.160 --> 00:15:39.500
Sane-yan, who are you talking to?

00:15:39.500 --> 00:15:40.160
Sane-yan?

00:15:40.170 --> 00:15:41.830
Er, Higashiyamato-san!

00:15:41.830 --> 00:15:44.840
"Sane-yan" appears to be a name
that only Zenjiro calls him by.

00:15:44.840 --> 00:15:47.840
Babbit is going to
call him that too. Sane-yan!

00:15:47.840 --> 00:15:49.170
Okay, Baby's Rock!

00:15:49.170 --> 00:15:51.180
Ah, Sana-chan!

00:15:51.180 --> 00:15:52.840
I fell!

00:15:52.850 --> 00:15:55.510
That's a shame, Sana-chan.
You can't go back to the basin anymore.

00:15:55.510 --> 00:15:56.510
No, I'm going back!

00:15:56.520 --> 00:16:00.550
If I go up to the second floor and
swing my way around, I'll get back!

00:16:03.190 --> 00:16:07.190
I did it! Water spilled
returned with a bang!

00:16:07.190 --> 00:16:10.190
I did it! I undid what was done!

00:16:10.200 --> 00:16:13.200
But still...

00:16:13.200 --> 00:16:14.870
Sensei, you know...

00:16:14.870 --> 00:16:17.200
...said that even if you don't know
what scars a person has on their hearts,

00:16:17.200 --> 00:16:18.540
you can still feel them,

00:16:18.540 --> 00:16:21.540
and that if you can convey to them
that you feel with them,

00:16:21.540 --> 00:16:25.880
Sana-chan, you might be able
to do something about it.

00:16:25.880 --> 00:16:27.210
I wonder if I can convey that.

00:16:27.210 --> 00:16:28.550
Sure you can!

00:16:28.550 --> 00:16:29.550
Really?

00:16:29.550 --> 00:16:30.880
Mm-hmm. You can.

00:16:30.880 --> 00:16:32.820
This week's Father Hayama.

00:16:31.340 --> 00:16:36.380
"Off"

00:16:32.820 --> 00:16:34.150
Papa-san?

00:16:34.150 --> 00:16:35.820
Oh, he's off, is he?

00:16:35.820 --> 00:16:37.490
Leave this to the pros!

00:16:37.490 --> 00:16:40.160
This week's Sana-chan!

00:16:40.160 --> 00:16:42.830
With a trophy for returning
spilled water to the basin!

00:16:42.830 --> 00:16:45.070
That should be about right.

00:16:46.170 --> 00:16:50.070
Kurosuke, during the next art class,
I'm going to the park to do sketches,

00:16:50.070 --> 00:16:51.170
so I'm going to leave
your water here for you.

00:16:51.170 --> 00:16:53.840
There's a straw coming out of it
so you don't drink too much, okay?

00:16:53.840 --> 00:16:56.170
You can only drink
as much as the straw will reach.

00:16:56.180 --> 00:16:57.840
Mami-chan, we're all going!

00:16:57.840 --> 00:17:01.190
--Ah, okay, I'm coming right now!
--Everyone, line up.

00:17:07.130 --> 00:17:09.130
"Let's draw pictures in the park"

00:17:07.190 --> 00:17:08.890
Mm, art in the fall...

00:17:13.860 --> 00:17:15.530
Hey, Mami-chan...

00:17:15.530 --> 00:17:18.530
I'm drawing Kurosuke!

00:17:18.530 --> 00:17:20.200
He looks like this, right?

00:17:20.200 --> 00:17:20.870
What?

00:17:20.870 --> 00:17:23.200
Sana-chan's Kurosuke looks like this.

00:17:23.200 --> 00:17:24.540
I guess it looks like him.

00:17:24.540 --> 00:17:26.840
Hmm, it needs something else.
Oh, I know!

00:17:26.840 --> 00:17:28.210
If I put a little spiral
on his tummy...!

00:17:28.210 --> 00:17:29.870
Kurosuke doesn't have one of those.

00:17:29.880 --> 00:17:30.880
No, he doesn't.

00:17:30.880 --> 00:17:32.480
Sana-chan, Mami-chan...

00:17:32.480 --> 00:17:33.480
What did you draw?

00:17:33.480 --> 00:17:34.810
I want to see, too.

00:17:34.810 --> 00:17:35.480
Kurosuke!

00:17:35.480 --> 00:17:38.820
Oh, how cute! Look, I drew
someone playing the saxophone.

00:17:38.820 --> 00:17:40.820
Me too!

00:17:40.820 --> 00:17:42.150
I wonder what Hisae-chan is drawing.

00:17:42.150 --> 00:17:42.820
Let's go see!

00:17:42.820 --> 00:17:43.820
Let's go!

00:17:43.820 --> 00:17:44.890
I'm drawing an

00:17:44.890 --> 00:17:48.160
"I have to play this game as a penalty
because I lost at billiards" person.

00:17:48.160 --> 00:17:52.160
--Here's mine.
--I drew this.

00:17:52.160 --> 00:17:55.870
Why doesn't anyone draw a landscape,
like normal?

00:17:55.870 --> 00:17:57.840
There's still some time,
so everyone draw another one.

00:17:57.840 --> 00:18:00.170
Hayama's not here!
He's playing hooky, huh?

00:18:00.170 --> 00:18:02.810
Yes, he is playing hooky.

00:18:07.180 --> 00:18:09.820
Don't drink too much water.

00:18:22.190 --> 00:18:23.530
Mami-chan, are you done?

00:18:23.530 --> 00:18:25.530
More or less. What about you, Sana-chan?

00:18:25.530 --> 00:18:29.200
Yeah, I'm done. I'm done,
but my colors seem to have run together.

00:18:29.200 --> 00:18:30.200
Amazing!

00:18:30.200 --> 00:18:31.540
Here's the picture.

00:18:31.540 --> 00:18:33.470
There's something alive
there in the middle, huh?

00:18:33.470 --> 00:18:34.810
That's a bench.

00:18:34.810 --> 00:18:36.550
Hayama, you paint something, too!

00:18:43.150 --> 00:18:46.150
Um, Kurata-san, I don't think you
should be walking too far out.

00:18:46.150 --> 00:18:50.150
--It could be dangerous if a car came.
--It's been two hours
since we've been away from the school!

00:18:50.160 --> 00:18:51.160
Hayama!

00:18:51.160 --> 00:18:54.660
Hey, what do you think
you're doing, cutting class!?

00:18:58.160 --> 00:18:58.830
Hey!

00:18:58.830 --> 00:19:00.500
What are you doing, out of nowhere!?

00:19:00.500 --> 00:19:01.830
The rab--

00:19:01.830 --> 00:19:02.500
The rab?

00:19:02.500 --> 00:19:04.710
--bit is acting strange.

00:19:07.170 --> 00:19:11.510
If I had only measured out your water,
you wouldn't have upset your stomach!

00:19:11.510 --> 00:19:14.850
Sometimes rabbits die
from diarrhea, don't they?

00:19:14.850 --> 00:19:19.520
But if it's diarrhea from drinking
too much water, they're okay, right?

00:19:19.520 --> 00:19:20.520
Hey!

00:19:20.520 --> 00:19:21.520
The veterinarian is here!

00:19:21.520 --> 00:19:23.190
Stop dawdling.

00:19:23.190 --> 00:19:25.260
Over here!

00:19:26.190 --> 00:19:28.530
He's gotten pretty weak, huh?

00:19:28.530 --> 00:19:32.460
I've taken what measures I can for now.
Make sure to keep him warm.

00:19:32.460 --> 00:19:33.460
Right.

00:19:33.470 --> 00:19:36.470
--Okay then--
--Can't you fix him up right, you quack?

00:19:36.470 --> 00:19:38.140
Who are you calling a quack!?

00:19:38.140 --> 00:19:41.470
I'm a first-rate doctor!
Who's a quack!? I'll kill you!

00:19:41.470 --> 00:19:44.480
Akito-kun, you've got me
caught in the middle, too! I'm flying!

00:19:44.480 --> 00:19:46.480
We haven't paid his consultation fee yet.

00:19:46.480 --> 00:19:47.810
Hayama...

00:19:47.810 --> 00:19:49.810
Can't you fix him up right?

00:19:49.820 --> 00:19:52.480
He's worried about Kurosuke, too.

00:19:52.480 --> 00:19:55.390
Babbit will refrain from making
any comments this time.

00:19:52.580 --> 00:19:55.540
"Kurosuke..."

00:19:55.390 --> 00:19:59.490
Okay, everyone, go on home now.
Let Sensei take it from here, okay?

00:19:59.490 --> 00:20:02.830
--Mami-chan, the folks at home
must be worried about you.
--Kurosuke...

00:20:02.830 --> 00:20:03.490
--What?

00:20:03.500 --> 00:20:07.830
Kurosuke! Kurosuke!

00:20:07.830 --> 00:20:09.540
Mami-chan!

00:20:15.510 --> 00:20:19.080
Mami-chan, let me hold Kurosuke.

00:20:24.520 --> 00:20:25.850
I feel so bad for you, Mami-chan.

00:20:25.850 --> 00:20:29.060
You can't help it
if he's dead, you know.

00:20:41.800 --> 00:20:44.140
Mami-chan!

00:20:44.140 --> 00:20:46.010
It's Kurosuke!

00:20:47.840 --> 00:20:50.840
Kurosuke!

00:20:50.840 --> 00:20:54.180
I'm sorry... Kurosuke, I'm sorry!

00:20:54.180 --> 00:20:56.380
--Mami-chan!
--That's great, Mami-chan!

00:20:58.850 --> 00:21:00.180
Hayama...

00:21:00.180 --> 00:21:02.850
Hayama, wait up!

00:21:02.850 --> 00:21:05.190
Bring something to feed
Kurosuke tomorrow morning.

00:21:05.190 --> 00:21:05.850
Why?

00:21:05.860 --> 00:21:09.020
Never mind, don't worry about it,
just do what I tell you.

00:21:09.030 --> 00:21:11.530
But just in case...

00:21:11.530 --> 00:21:14.160
Just in case things get
messed up even worse than before,

00:21:14.160 --> 00:21:17.200
then you can hold it against me
for the rest of your life, okay?

00:21:17.200 --> 00:21:22.200
--Just go and, ba-bing, bring some food
to the rabbit hutch, okay?
--Huh?

00:21:22.380 --> 00:21:24.840
"Just in case?"

00:21:22.540 --> 00:21:24.680
I was about to say something,
but I forgot what it was.

00:21:29.210 --> 00:21:30.550
Melon.

00:21:30.550 --> 00:21:32.550
Just a second.

00:21:32.550 --> 00:21:35.550
Can I give this to him?

00:21:35.550 --> 00:21:36.220
No.

00:21:36.220 --> 00:21:39.220
Oh. Never mind.

00:21:42.230 --> 00:21:46.560
If you give him that much to eat at once,
you're going to upset his stomach again.

00:21:46.560 --> 00:21:49.630
Oh, is that right?

00:21:53.840 --> 00:21:55.650
You...

00:21:57.170 --> 00:21:59.020
...and the rabbit...

00:21:59.840 --> 00:22:02.050
...are both pretty strong.

00:22:13.860 --> 00:22:15.800
You forgot your melon.

00:22:21.860 --> 00:22:23.870
Hayama!

00:22:23.870 --> 00:22:25.870
Did you bring Kurosuke something to eat?

00:22:25.870 --> 00:22:26.530
Yeah.

00:22:26.540 --> 00:22:30.210
You did? You did? You did?

00:22:30.210 --> 00:22:33.210
Oh, you're playing Tanuki, huh?

00:22:33.210 --> 00:22:37.210
Mami-chan appears to be doing fine, too!

00:22:37.210 --> 00:22:40.550
Maybe I'll sing!

00:22:40.750 --> 00:22:42.210
"Back against the wall."

00:22:42.710 --> 00:22:47.720
That's what you say about times like these.

00:22:48.970 --> 00:22:52.470
In dire straits,

00:22:53.220 --> 00:22:56.060
I've been waiting for an answer.

00:22:56.560 --> 00:22:59.940
My confessions are worked out
long in advance,

00:23:00.900 --> 00:23:05.030
to always go along with the scenario.

00:23:05.230 --> 00:23:11.070
My heart may be settled, but my mind is in a...

00:23:11.320 --> 00:23:13.280
...panic!!

00:23:14.280 --> 00:23:19.120
When my friends invite me by, suddenly,

00:23:19.330 --> 00:23:21.830
he's there.

00:23:22.750 --> 00:23:25.090
And our usual classroom...

00:23:25.300 --> 00:23:27.670
...quick-changes into a merry-go-round...

00:23:27.760 --> 00:23:30.180
...for two.

00:23:31.010 --> 00:23:33.640
Although I've said nothing but wisecracks...

00:23:33.850 --> 00:23:38.390
...up to now, just for today,

00:23:39.310 --> 00:23:41.980
I'm going to be honest and sincere,

00:23:42.190 --> 00:23:46.690
so BOY, take a look my way!

00:23:47.610 --> 00:23:52.280
When my friends invite me by, suddenly,

00:23:52.450 --> 00:23:54.950
he's there,

00:23:55.910 --> 00:23:58.160
And our usual classroom...

00:23:58.410 --> 00:24:00.660
...quick-changes into a merry-go-round...

00:24:00.830 --> 00:24:03.210
...for two.

00:24:06.800 --> 00:24:09.470
Hoy! In Sana-chan's next adventures...

00:24:09.470 --> 00:24:11.970
I'd forgotten all about it!
Do you guys remember?

00:24:11.970 --> 00:24:13.480
The chick that I gave to Aono-chan?

00:24:13.480 --> 00:24:16.810
Huh? Who's Aono-chan? You're being a
little too forgetful there, sir!

00:24:16.810 --> 00:24:20.150
Time sure does fly. The chick
has now become a fine rooster!

00:24:20.150 --> 00:24:23.490
However, this creates a huge problem!
Living in the city sure is hard!

00:24:23.490 --> 00:24:27.820
Next time on Kodomo no Omocha, Episode 26,
the Rub Those Sleepy Eyes and Dizzy Head saga,

00:24:27.820 --> 00:24:31.490
Cock-a-Doodle-Doo, Morning is Coming

00:24:31.490 --> 00:24:35.030
It's going to be absol-oodle-doo...
I'm too sleepy...
